WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.875 --> 00:00:01.980
(techno music)

00:00:01.980 --> 00:00:03.415
- We will see a transgender Olympian,

00:00:03.415 --> 00:00:04.565
in my lifetime.

00:00:04.565 --> 00:00:07.665
Someone who is out and
authentic with their identity

00:00:07.665 --> 00:00:10.240
and still competing in
sports at a high level,

00:00:10.240 --> 00:00:12.407
because now it's possible.

00:00:13.797 --> 00:00:14.994
My name is Chris Mosier

00:00:14.994 --> 00:00:16.452
and I'm the first transgender man

00:00:16.452 --> 00:00:19.024
to make a men's US National Team.

00:00:19.024 --> 00:00:21.256
My sport is sprint duathlon.

00:00:21.256 --> 00:00:23.839
And duathlon is run, bike, run.

00:00:24.907 --> 00:00:27.738
When I first started
competing after transition,

00:00:27.738 --> 00:00:29.956
No one really thought
that I would do well.

00:00:29.956 --> 00:00:31.629
Everyone pretty much just wrote me off

00:00:31.629 --> 00:00:33.224
because they looked at me

00:00:33.224 --> 00:00:35.163
and thought, "Oh, he's a trans guy.

00:00:35.163 --> 00:00:38.345
"There's no way that he
can compete against men."

00:00:38.345 --> 00:00:40.927
Hearing people say that
really motivated me

00:00:40.927 --> 00:00:43.624
to work harder, to learn more,

00:00:43.624 --> 00:00:45.960
to be more dedicated to my training

00:00:45.960 --> 00:00:50.721
and try to be the strongest
competitor that I can be.

00:00:50.721 --> 00:00:52.368
Even though I made Team USA,

00:00:52.368 --> 00:00:54.338
I was ineligible to
compete at the world level

00:00:54.338 --> 00:00:56.523
because of the International
Olympic Committee policy

00:00:56.523 --> 00:00:59.021
which stated transgender
athletes needed to have

00:00:59.021 --> 00:01:02.972
a full lower surgery
performed in order to qualify.

00:01:02.972 --> 00:01:05.594
Adding an extra body part
is not going to make me

00:01:05.594 --> 00:01:08.838
a faster runner or a stronger cyclist.

00:01:08.838 --> 00:01:12.049
They just needed an athlete
with a name and a face,

00:01:12.049 --> 00:01:14.737
someone who was actually
being impacted by this policy

00:01:14.737 --> 00:01:17.930
to look at it and to say this isn't right.

00:01:17.930 --> 00:01:20.350
The International Olympic
Committee changed their policy

00:01:20.350 --> 00:01:22.210
for transgender athletes
and no longer have

00:01:22.210 --> 00:01:25.237
the same restrictions they had before.

00:01:25.237 --> 00:01:28.707
I was so thrilled when the
policy was changed for myself,

00:01:28.707 --> 00:01:31.547
but I was even happier that
the policy is now changed

00:01:31.547 --> 00:01:33.738
for everybody who comes after me.

00:01:33.738 --> 00:01:35.176
I will not be competing in Rio

00:01:35.176 --> 00:01:37.652
because duathlon is not an Olympic sport,

00:01:37.652 --> 00:01:39.547
but I am so excited to some day

00:01:39.547 --> 00:01:41.600
see a transgender Olympian compete

00:01:41.600 --> 00:01:43.361
on behalf of our country.

00:01:43.361 --> 00:01:47.111
What used to be the
ceiling is now the floor.

